              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "せつやくする — setsuyaku suru — \"to economize; to save (energy, money)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "でんきが たかいので、せつやくしています。 — denki ga takai node, setsuyaku shite imasu — \"Electricity is expensive, so we are cutting down.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Polite せつやくします, setsuyakushimasu; a する verb. Past (polite): ははが みずを せつやくしました。, haha ga mizu o setsuyaku shimashita."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "せつやくする (setsuyaku suru) is built from a Sino-Japanese noun and the native verb suru, \"to do\". The noun, setsuyaku, is two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese: setsu, \"joint\" (Middle Chinese tset) and yaku, \"shrink\" ('jak) (KANJIDIC2; JMdict; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
            }
          ]
        },
